{"id":"GHSA-2xwh-426q-42c5","axis":"advisories","repo":"kubeflow/pipelines","sha":"620d0cc89ae0d042a484a003f8ffe6e9a55d347e","parsed":{"files":[{"path":"backend/src/cache/README.md","lines":["@@ -1,3 +1,64 @@","+## Namespace isolation and upgrades","+","+This service caches legacy V1/raw-Argo steps. Standard V2 component pods bypass","+this webhook cache; their cache implementation is separate.","+","+By default, cache reuse is restricted to the pod's Kubernetes namespace. Database","+namespace filtering enforces isolation; including the namespace in the cache key","+provides an additional safeguard. Admission derives the key from the API server's","+request namespace and the selected Argo template fields. On completion, the","+watcher recomputes the key from the observed pod's namespace and template instead","+of trusting its mutable cache-key annotation. This does not establish an integrity","+boundary between users who can modify workloads in the same namespace.","+","+Upgrading adds a `Namespace` column and a namespace/key index automatically at","+cache-server startup. Existing rows retain an empty namespace and are not reused","+by default because their ownership cannot be safely inferred. Do not backfill","+them. Normal expiry still applies to these rows.","+","+Stop all old cache-server replicas before bringing up the fixed version, and","+coordinate the webhook outage with workload submission. A mixed-version rollout","+does not provide the new isolation guarantee. Allow startup migration to complete","+before resuming submissions. Expect a cold cache, extra step executions, and","+additional resource use; pre-upgrade pods with old-format keys do not seed the new","+cache. Do not roll back to the vulnerable implementation to recover cache hits.","+","+### Optional legacy-cache fallback","+","+Administrators can set `ALLOW_LEGACY_CACHE_FALLBACK=true` for a bounded upgrade","+period. The default is `false` when unset. After a namespaced cache miss, this","+option permits a lookup using the original template-only hash, restricted to","+legacy rows with `Namespace = ''`. Normal namespace validation, namespace-scoped","+reads and writes, cache expiry, and disabled-cache behavior remain enforced.","+","+Enabling this option accepts possible reuse of another tenant's historical","+outputs, including poisoned outputs, because legacy row ownership is unknown.","+The full namespace isolation guarantee applies only with the fallback disabled.","+Stopping old replicas before upgrading is still required.","+","+For a deployment in the `kubeflow` namespace (adjust `NAMESPACE` as needed):","+","+```sh","+NAMESPACE=kubeflow","+kubectl set env deployment/cache-server -n \"$NAMESPACE\" ALLOW_LEGACY_CACHE_FALLBACK=true","+```","+","+Legacy hits do not populate the new namespaced cache, and no automatic promotion","+or backfill occurs. Turning off the option can therefore still cause cold-cache","+executions. Disable it after the planned upgrade period:","+","+```sh","+kubectl set env deployment/cache-server -n \"$NAMESPACE\" ALLOW_LEGACY_CACHE_FALLBACK=false","+```","+","+The migration/storage regression runs with SQLite in the normal cache test suite.","+To also exercise MySQL and PostgreSQL, set `KFP_CACHE_TEST_MYSQL_DSN` and","+`KFP_CACHE_TEST_POSTGRES_DSN` to empty disposable test databases and run:","+","+```sh","+go test ./backend/src/cache/storage -run TestCacheNamespaceMigrationAndStorage -count=1","+```","+"," ## Build src image"," To build the Docker image of cache server, run the following Docker command from the pipelines directory:"," "],"additions":61,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"backend/src/cache/model/execution_cache.go","lines":["@@ -16,12 +16,14 @@ package model"," "," type ExecutionCache struct {"," \tID                int64  `gorm:\"column:ID; not null; primaryKey; AUTO_INCREMENT; index:composite_id_idx\"`","-\tExecutionCacheKey string `gorm:\"column:ExecutionCacheKey; not null; index:idx_cache_key;\"`","+\tExecutionCacheKey string `gorm:\"column:ExecutionCacheKey; not null; index:idx_cache_key; index:idx_cache_namespace_key,priority:2;\"`"," \tExecutionTemplate string `gorm:\"column:ExecutionTemplate; not null;\"`"," \tExecutionOutput   string `gorm:\"column:ExecutionOutput; not null;\"`"," \tMaxCacheStaleness int64  `gorm:\"column:MaxCacheStaleness; not null;\"`"," \tStartedAtInSec    int64  `gorm:\"column:StartedAtInSec; not null; index:composite_id_idx;\"`"," \tEndedAtInSec      int64  `gorm:\"column:EndedAtInSec; not null;\"`","+\t// Empty namespace marks legacy rows whose tenant ownership cannot be established.","+\tNamespace string `gorm:\"column:Namespace; size:63; not null; default:''; index:idx_cache_namespace_key,priority:1;\"`"," }"," "," // GetValueOfPrimaryKey returns the value of ExecutionCacheKey."],"additions":3,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"backend/src/cache/server/legacy_fallback_test.go","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,193 @@","+// Copyright 2026 The Kubeflow Authors","+//","+// Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (the \"License\");","+// you may not use this file except in compliance with the License.","+// You may obtain a copy of the License at","+//","+// https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0","+//","+// Unless required by applicable law or agreed to in writing, software","+// distributed under the License is distributed on an \"AS IS\" BASIS,","+// WITHOUT WARRANTIES OR CONDITIONS OF ANY KIND, either express or implied.","+// See the License for the specific language governing permissions and","+// limitations under the License.","+","+package server","+","+import (","+\t\"context\"","+\t\"encoding/json\"","+\t\"errors\"","+\t\"fmt\"","+\t\"os\"","+\t\"testing\"","+\t\"time\"","+","+\t\"github.com/kubeflow/pipelines/backend/src/cache/model\"","+\t\"github.com/kubeflow/pipelines/backend/src/cache/storage\"","+\t\"github.com/kubeflow/pipelines/backend/src/common/util\"","+\t\"github.com/stretchr/testify/require\"","+)","+","+func legacyCacheManager(t *testing.T) *FakeClientManager {","+\tt.Helper()","+\tm, err := NewFakeClientManager(util.NewFakeTime(time.Unix(100, 0)))","+\trequire.NoError(t, err)","+\tt.Cleanup(func() { require.NoError(t, m.Close()) })","+\treturn m","+}","+","+func legacyCacheRow(t *testing.T) *model.ExecutionCache {","+\tt.Helper()","+\ttemplate, ok := getArgoTemplate(fakePod)","+\trequire.True(t, ok)","+\tkey, err := generateLegacyCacheKeyFromTemplate(template)","+\trequire.NoError(t, err)","+\t// Pin the pre-upgrade hash so the fallback cannot silently use the new format.","+\trequire.Equal(t, \"07f2c42567af4f141a52887e0a113c9aefdfdfd5e6b06b9908f7fdb0b43739af\", key)","+\toutput, err := json.Marshal(map[string]string{ArgoWorkflowOutputs: cachePod(\"tenant\").Annotations[ArgoWorkflowOutputs]})","+\trequire.NoError(t, err)","+\treturn &model.ExecutionCache{","+\t\tExecutionCacheKey: key,","+\t\tExecutionTemplate: template,","+\t\tExecutionOutput:   string(output),","+\t\tMaxCacheStaleness: -1,","+\t\tStartedAtInSec:    1,","+\t\tEndedAtInSec:      2,","+\t}","+}","+","+func TestLegacyCacheFallbackAdmission(t *testing.T) {","+\tfor _, tc := range []struct {","+\t\tname         string","+\t\tsetting      string","+\t\tnamespace    string","+\t\tpodTTL       string","+\t\tdefaultTTL   string","+\t\tmaximumTTL   string","+\t\trowExpired   bool","+\t\twantHit      bool","+\t\twantRowCount int64","+\t}{","+\t\t{name: \"unset by default\", wantRowCount: 1},","+\t\t{name: \"explicitly disabled\", setting: \"false\", wantRowCount: 1},","+\t\t{name: \"legacy hit\", setting: \"true\", wantHit: true, wantRowCount: 1},","+\t\t{name: \"another namespace excluded\", setting: \"true\", namespace: \"other\", wantRowCount: 1},","+\t\t{name: \"pod caching disabled\", setting: \"true\", podTTL: \"P0D\", wantRowCount: 1},","+\t\t{name: \"default caching disabled\", setting: \"true\", defaultTTL: \"P0D\", wantRowCount: 1},","+\t\t{name: \"pod TTL expired\", setting: \"true\", podTTL: \"PT1S\", wantRowCount: 1},","+\t\t{name: \"default TTL expired\", setting: \"true\", defaultTTL: \"PT1S\", wantRowCount: 1},","+\t\t{name: \"row TTL expired\", setting: \"true\", rowExpired: true, wantRowCount: 1},","+\t\t{name: \"maximum TTL expired\", setting: \"true\", maximumTTL: \"PT1S\"},","+\t} {","+\t\tt.Run(tc.name, func(t *testing.T) {","+\t\t\tt.Setenv(\"ALLOW_LEGACY_CACHE_FALLBACK\", tc.setting)","+\t\t\tif tc.setting == \"\" {","+\t\t\t\trequire.NoError(t, os.Unsetenv(\"ALLOW_LEGACY_CACHE_FALLBACK\"))","+\t\t\t}","+\t\t\tt.Setenv(\"DEFAULT_CACHE_STALENESS\", tc.defaultTTL)","+\t\t\tt.Setenv(\"MAXIMUM_CACHE_STALENESS\", tc.maximumTTL)","+\t\t\t// The fallback setting must be independent of this existing boolean option.","+\t\t\tt.Setenv(\"CACHE_NODE_RESTRICTIONS\", \"true\")","+\t\t\tm := legacyCacheManager(t)","+\t\t\trow := legacyCacheRow(t)","+\t\t\trow.Namespace = tc.namespace","+\t\t\tif tc.rowExpired {","+\t\t\t\trow.MaxCacheStaleness = 1","+\t\t\t}","+\t\t\trequire.NoError(t, m.DB().Create(row).Error)","+\t\t\tp := cachePod(\"tenant\")","+\t\t\tif tc.podTTL != \"\" {","+\t\t\t\tp.Annotations[MaxCacheStalenessKey] = tc.podTTL","+\t\t\t}","+\t\t\trequire.Equal(t, tc.wantHit, admitCachePod(t, p, m))","+\t\t\tif tc.wantHit {","+\t\t\t\trequire.Equal(t, getValueFromSerializedMap(row.ExecutionOutput, ArgoWorkflowOutputs), p.Annotations[ArgoWorkflowOutputs])","+\t\t\t\t// A legacy hit is not promoted or given a fresh age by the watcher.","+\t\t\t\trequire.NoError(t, cacheCompletedPod(context.Background(), p, m))","+\t\t\t\tvar retained model.ExecutionCache","+\t\t\t\trequire.NoError(t, m.DB().First(&retained, row.ID).Error)","+\t\t\t\trequire.Equal(t, *row, retained)","+\t\t\t}","+\t\t\tvar rows int64","+\t\t\trequire.NoError(t, m.DB().Model(&model.ExecutionCache{}).Count(&rows).Error)","+\t\t\trequire.Equal(t, tc.wantRowCount, rows)","+\t\t})","+\t}","+}","+","+func TestLegacyCacheFallbackPreservesScopedWritesAndHitPrecedence(t *testing.T) {","+\tm := legacyCacheManager(t)","+\tlegacy := legacyCacheRow(t)","+\trequire.NoError(t, m.DB().Create(legacy).Error)","+\tt.Setenv(\"ALLOW_LEGACY_CACHE_FALLBACK\", \"false\")","+\tp := cachePod(\"tenant\")","+\trequire.False(t, admitCachePod(t, p, m))","+","+\tt.Setenv(\"ALLOW_LEGACY_CACHE_FALLBACK\", \"true\")","+\tt.Setenv(\"CACHE_NODE_RESTRICTIONS\", \"false\")","+\tp.Annotations[ArgoWorkflowOutputs] = `{\"parameters\":[{\"name\":\"result\",\"value\":\"scoped-output\"}]}`","+\trequire.NoError(t, cacheCompletedPod(context.Background(), p, m))","+\tnext := cachePod(\"tenant\")","+\trequire.True(t, admitCachePod(t, next, m))","+\trequire.Equal(t, p.Annotations[ArgoWorkflowOutputs], next.Annotations[ArgoWorkflowOutputs])","+\tvar rows []model.ExecutionCache","+\trequire.NoError(t, m.DB().Order(\"ID\").Find(&rows).Error)","+\trequire.Len(t, rows, 2)","+\trequire.Equal(t, *legacy, rows[0])","+\trequire.Equal(t, \"tenant\", rows[1].Namespace)","+\trequire.NotEqual(t, legacy.ExecutionCacheKey, rows[1].ExecutionCacheKey)","+}","+","+func TestLegacyCacheFallbackInvalidConfiguration(t *testing.T) {","+\tt.Setenv(\"ALLOW_LEGACY_CACHE_FALLBACK\", \"invalid\")","+\tm := legacyCacheManager(t)","+\trequire.NoError(t, m.DB().Create(legacyCacheRow(t)).Error)","+\tp := cachePod(\"tenant\")","+\treq := GetFakeRequestFromPod(p)","+\treq.Namespace = p.Namespace","+\tpatches, err := MutatePodIfCached(req, m)","+\trequire.ErrorContains(t, err, \"ALLOW_LEGACY_CACHE_FALLBACK\")","+\trequire.Empty(t, patches)","+}","+","+type scopedLookupErrorStore struct {","+\tstorage.ExecutionCacheStoreInterface","+\tlookupErr   error","+\tlegacyReads int","+}","+","+func (s *scopedLookupErrorStore) GetExecutionCache(string, string, int64, int64) (*model.ExecutionCache, error) {","+\treturn nil, s.lookupErr","+}","+","+func (s *scopedLookupErrorStore) GetLegacyExecutionCache(key string, staleness, maximumStaleness int64) (*model.ExecutionCache, error) {","+\ts.legacyReads++","+\treturn s.ExecutionCacheStoreInterface.GetLegacyExecutionCache(key, staleness, maximumStaleness)","+}","+","+func TestLegacyCacheFallbackOnlyAfterCacheMiss(t *testing.T) {","+\tt.Setenv(\"ALLOW_LEGACY_CACHE_FALLBACK\", \"true\")","+\tfor _, tc := range []struct {","+\t\tname    string","+\t\terr     error","+\t\twantHit bool","+\t}{","+\t\t{\"database read error\", errors.New(\"database read failed\"), false},","+\t\t{\"database cleanup error\", errors.New(\"database cleanup failed\"), false},","+\t\t{\"wrapped cache miss\", fmt.Errorf(\"lookup: %w\", storage.ErrExecutionCacheNotFound), true},","+\t} {","+\t\tt.Run(tc.name, func(t *testing.T) {","+\t\t\tm := legacyCacheManager(t)","+\t\t\trequire.NoError(t, m.DB().Create(legacyCacheRow(t)).Error)","+\t\t\ts := &scopedLookupErrorStore{ExecutionCacheStoreInterface: m.CacheStore(), lookupErr: tc.err}","+\t\t\tm.cacheStore = s","+\t\t\trequire.Equal(t, tc.wantHit, admitCachePod(t, cachePod(\"tenant\"), m))","+\t\t\tif tc.wantHit {","+\t\t\t\trequire.Equal(t, 1, s.legacyReads)","+\t\t\t} else {","+\t\t\t\trequire.Zero(t, s.legacyReads)","+\t\t\t}","+\t\t})","+\t}","+}"],"additions":193,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"backend/src/cache/server/mutation.go","lines":["@@ -18,6 +18,7 @@ import ("," \t\"crypto/sha256\""," \t\"encoding/hex\""," \t\"encoding/json\"","+\t\"errors\""," \t\"fmt\""," \t\"log\""," \t\"os\"","@@ -99,6 +100,11 @@ func MutatePodIfCached(req *v1beta1.AdmissionRequest, clientMgr ClientManagerInt"," \t\tlog.Printf(\"This pod %s is created by KFP v2 pipelines.\", pod.ObjectMeta.Name)"," \t\treturn nil, nil"," \t}","+\t// Namespace comes from the API server's admission context, not caller metadata.","+\tif req.Namespace == \"\" || (pod.Namespace != \"\" && pod.Namespace != req.Namespace) {","+\t\tlog.Printf(\"Skipping cache lookup for pod %s: missing or inconsistent namespace\", pod.Name)","+\t\treturn nil, nil","+\t}"," "," \tvar patches []patchOperation"," \tannotations := pod.ObjectMeta.Annotations","@@ -110,7 +116,8 @@ func MutatePodIfCached(req *v1beta1.AdmissionRequest, clientMgr ClientManagerInt"," \t}"," "," \t// Generate the executionHashKey based on pod.metadata.annotations.workflows.argoproj.io/template","-\texecutionHashKey, err := generateCacheKeyFromTemplate(template)","+\t// and the pod's namespace, so cache entries are scoped to a single tenant.","+\texecutionHashKey, err := generateCacheKeyFromTemplate(template, req.Namespace)"," \tlog.Println(executionHashKey)"," \tif err != nil {"," \t\tlog.Printf(\"Unable to generate cache key for pod %s : %s\", pod.ObjectMeta.Name, err.Error())","@@ -149,7 +156,23 @@ func MutatePodIfCached(req *v1beta1.AdmissionRequest, clientMgr ClientManagerInt"," \tlog.Printf(\"cacheStalenessInSeconds: %d\", cacheStalenessInSeconds)"," "," \tvar cachedExecution *model.ExecutionCache","-\tcachedExecution, err = clientMgr.CacheStore().GetExecutionCache(executionHashKey, cacheStalenessInSeconds, maximumCacheStalenessInSeconds)","+\tcachedExecution, err = clientMgr.CacheStore().GetExecutionCache(req.Namespace, executionHashKey, cacheStalenessInSeconds, maximumCacheStalenessInSeconds)","+\tif errors.Is(err, storage.ErrExecutionCacheNotFound) {","+\t\tallowLegacyFallback, configErr := getEnvBool(\"ALLOW_LEGACY_CACHE_FALLBACK\")","+\t\tif configErr != nil {","+\t\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"invalid ALLOW_LEGACY_CACHE_FALLBACK: set it to true or false: %w\", configErr)","+\t\t}","+\t\tif allowLegacyFallback {","+\t\t\tlegacyKey, keyErr := generateLegacyCacheKeyFromTemplate(template)","+\t\t\tif keyErr != nil {","+\t\t\t\treturn nil, keyErr","+\t\t\t}","+\t\t\tcachedExecution, err = clientMgr.CacheStore().GetLegacyExecutionCache(legacyKey, cacheStalenessInSeconds, maximumCacheStalenessInSeconds)","+\t\t\tif cachedExecution != nil {","+\t\t\t\tlog.Printf(\"Using legacy cache entry %d for pod %s/%s: original namespace is unknown; ALLOW_LEGACY_CACHE_FALLBACK is enabled\", cachedExecution.ID, req.Namespace, pod.Name)","+\t\t\t}","+\t\t}","+\t}"," \tif err != nil {"," \t\tlog.Println(err.Error())"," \t}","@@ -235,26 +258,68 @@ func MutatePodIfCached(req *v1beta1.AdmissionRequest, clientMgr ClientManagerInt"," "," // intersectStructureWithSkeleton recursively intersects two maps"," // nil values in the skeleton map mean that the whole value (which can also be a map) should be kept.","-func intersectStructureWithSkeleton(src map[string]interface{}, skeleton map[string]interface{}) map[string]interface{} {","+func intersectStructureWithSkeleton(src map[string]interface{}, skeleton map[string]interface{}) (map[string]interface{}, error) {"," \tresult := make(map[string]interface{})"," \tfor key, skeletonValue := range skeleton {"," \t\tif value, ok := src[key]; ok {"," \t\t\tif skeletonValue == nil {"," \t\t\t\tresult[key] = value"," \t\t\t} else {","-\t\t\t\tresult[key] = intersectStructureWithSkeleton(value.(map[string]interface{}), skeletonValue.(map[string]interface{}))","+\t\t\t\tobject, ok := value.(map[string]interface{})","+\t\t\t\tif !ok || object == nil {","+\t\t\t\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"template field %q must be a JSON object\", key)","+\t\t\t\t}","+\t\t\t\tnestedSkeleton, ok := skeletonValue.(map[string]interface{})","+\t\t\t\tif !ok {","+\t\t\t\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"cache skeleton field %q must be an object or nil\", key)","+\t\t\t\t}","+\t\t\t\tnested, err := intersectStructureWithSkeleton(object, nestedSkeleton)","+\t\t\t\tif err != nil {","+\t\t\t\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"template field %q: %w\", key, err)","+\t\t\t\t}","+\t\t\t\tresult[key] = nested"," \t\t\t}"," \t\t}"," \t}","-\treturn result","+\treturn result, nil"," }"," ","-func generateCacheKeyFromTemplate(template string) (string, error) {","+func generateCacheKeyFromTemplate(template string, namespace string) (string, error) {","+\tif namespace == \"\" {","+\t\treturn \"\", fmt.Errorf(\"cache key requires a pod namespace\")","+\t}","+\tcacheKeyMap, err := filterTemplateForCacheKey(template)","+\tif err != nil {","+\t\treturn \"\", err","+\t}","+","+\t// Database namespace predicates enforce ownership. Including the trusted","+\t// namespace in the hash also keeps tenant identities distinct if a future","+\t// lookup accidentally omits its namespace predicate.","+\treturn hashCacheKey(map[string]interface{}{","+\t\t\"namespace\": namespace,","+\t\t\"template\":  cacheKeyMap,","+\t})","+}","+","+// generateLegacyCacheKeyFromTemplate reproduces the pre-namespace key for legacy-only reads.","+func generateLegacyCacheKeyFromTemplate(template string) (string, error) {","+\tcacheKeyMap, err := filterTemplateForCacheKey(template)","+\tif err != nil {","+\t\treturn \"\", err","+\t}","+\treturn hashCacheKey(cacheKeyMap)","+}","+","+func filterTemplateForCacheKey(template string) (map[string]interface{}, error) {"," \tvar templateMap map[string]interface{}"," \tb := []byte(template)"," \terr := json.Unmarshal(b, &templateMap)"," \tif err != nil {","-\t\treturn \"\", err","+\t\treturn nil, err","+\t}","+\tif templateMap == nil {","+\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"cache template must be a JSON object, not null\")"," \t}"," "," \t// Selectively copying parts of the template that should affect the cache","@@ -272,9 +337,12 @@ func generateCacheKeyFromTemplate(template string) (string, error) {"," \t\t\"initContainers\": nil,"," \t\t\"sidecars\":       nil,"," \t}","-\tcacheKeyMap := intersectStructureWithSkeleton(templateMap, templateSkeleton)","+\treturn intersectStructureWithSkeleton(templateMap, templateSkeleton)","+}"," ","-\tb, err = json.Marshal(cacheKeyMap)","+func hashCacheKey(keyedStructure map[string]interface{}) (string, error) {","+\t// encoding/json.Marshal documents sorted map keys, including nested maps.","+\tb, err := json.Marshal(keyedStructure)"," \tif err != nil {"," \t\treturn \"\", err"," \t}","@@ -340,7 +408,7 @@ func isV2Pod(pod *corev1.Pod) bool {"," }"," "," func getEnvBool(key string) (bool, error) {","-\tv, ok := os.LookupEnv(\"CACHE_NODE_RESTRICTIONS\")","+\tv, ok := os.LookupEnv(key)"," \tif !